# C02 persistence review evidence

`DESIGN.md` compares two storage/wire approaches and proposes a bounded additive adapter slice. No proposal was applied to shared source.

The actual probe command, from this scratch directory, was:

```sh
/private/tmp/zodiacs-platform-runtime/node_modules/node/bin/node \
  /Users/chiburashka/.codex/worktrees/4806/site/node_modules/vitest/vitest.mjs run \
  --config vitest.config.mjs --reporter=verbose --reporter=json \
  --outputFile.json=result.json > probe.log 2>&1
```

Runtime: Node 22.23.2, Vitest 3.2.6, ICU 78.2, tzdata 2026a. Exit code 1 is intentional: **two red assertions reproduce active request-loss/identity defects; three controls pass**. `result.json` and `probe.log` are the exact test outputs. `observations.json` records fields and source hashes without a real-user fixture.

`identity.json` records observed site HEAD `921cd0d16cd0c4a82692d311c3af326b0045531d`, active engine `0.1.1-rc.1`, and calculation-entry hashes. Probe SHA256: `78f74df73c10d0b0490743e579a8af951328f842782d6178d4378a852e320313`; result SHA256: `899de7cb4cd2c763fe13e26fdca56c8921664543d0cdb4b413da8e5d7b8f71ae`; observations SHA256: `c97597a9e5520e5ce637f363d99eecb18d65d297c21cd8b23bfc740aa1bd4e56`.

The probe imports actual current site `computeChart`, profile store/read/handoff and account wire/fingerprint functions. Its synthetic SavedChart construction mirrors the current `ChartCalculator.commitSave` projection and checks that source mapping remains present; it does not drive the calculator browser UI. Memory storage, synthetic UUIDs/labels/dates and a blocked fetch stub are used. No real browser storage, account, database, network request, shared file, server flag or release state was changed.

The two failed expectations are: requested Placidus should replay as Placidus (actual Whole); and saving a separate explicit Whole request should insert a second chart (actual update of the first). The three passing controls establish unsafe same-key version bump, field-dropping old-client re-save, and indistinguishable v1 wire bytes/fingerprints. Passing those controls demonstrates limitations; it does not assert either storage proposal is implemented.
